---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "ProfilePage",
      "mainEntity": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Hassam Shabbir",
        "url": "https://behavioralpsychology.pro/author/hassam-shabbir/",
        "image": "https://behavioralpsychology.pro/images/author-hassam-shabbir.webp",
        "jobTitle": "Psychologist, Writer and Author",
        "sameAs": [
          "https://www.instagram.com/hassam_shabbir_official/",
          "https://www.threads.net/@hassam_shabbir_official",
          "https://www.linkedin.com/in/hassam-shabbir-sxo/"
        ],
        "description": "Hassam Shabbir is the psychologist, writer and author behind Behavioral Psychology."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hassam Shabbir: Psychologist, Writer and Author Bio"
  description="Hassam Shabbir is the psychologist, writer and author behind Behavioral Psychology. Read his first-person profile, editorial role, and credentials."
  ogImage="/images/author-hassam-shabbir.webp"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <span>Author</span></p>
      <p class="kicker">Professional profile</p>
      <h1>Hassam Shabbir | Psychologist, Writer and Author</h1>
      <p>I am the psychologist, writer, and author behind Behavioral Psychology. Every article on this site is written by me, in my own words, and checked against the sources I cite.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p style="text-align:center; margin-bottom:28px;">
          <img
            src="/images/author-hassam-shabbir.webp"
            alt="Portrait of Hassam Shabbir"
            width="400"
            height="400"
            style="border-radius:50%; max-width:280px; height:auto;"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </p>

        <h2>Psychology training shaped by the responsibility to explain</h2>
        <p>My formal psychology education began in Pakistan with a B.S. in Psychology from the University of Sargodha, where I developed a lasting interest in how behavior is shaped, how habits form, and how environments influence the choices people make. That interest never left me. It continued through professional study from institutions in the United States and Canada, covering abnormal psychology, behavioral change, psychosis, relationships, and school mental health, and it runs through everything I write.</p>
        <p>My professional work is remote and international, including projects and clients in the United States. It centers on research, writing, content strategy, and psychology-informed communication for complex health and education topics. My broader writing portfolio includes more than 1,000 articles across healthcare, education, technology, and other fields.</p>
        <p>As founder of Rise Above Minds, I lead a nonprofit initiative that shares mental health and psychology education with children and communities. I have also trained more than 400 professionals in AI and prompt engineering. Teaching sharpened my writing: when you have to explain a complex idea to a room full of people with different backgrounds, you learn quickly what works and what does not. I write every article on this site the way I would teach it, starting simple, building up, and never hiding behind terminology.</p>

        <h2>A clear claim with a clear boundary</h2>
        <p>This profile documents my editorial role, completed learning, and selected work. Course certificates listed below are presented as continued study, not as a degree, professional license, or specialty certification.</p>
        <p>What I do: I write educational articles about behavioral psychology, I research degrees and career routes so readers can compare them honestly, and I review evidence and sources for this publication before anything is published.</p>
        <p>What I do not do through this publication: I do not diagnose conditions, I do not give treatment advice, and I do not provide clinical care. Nothing on this site creates a psychologist-patient relationship, and nothing here should be used to diagnose or treat any condition.</p>

        <h2>The subjects behind the byline</h2>
        <p>My writing on this publication stays inside four areas of focus. These describe the educational topics I research and explain; they do not replace case-specific assessment or professional advice.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Behavioral psychology fundamentals: learning, conditioning, reinforcement, and how behavior is studied.</li>
          <li>Behavior change in everyday life: habits, health, classrooms, and workplaces.</li>
          <li>Degrees and careers: honest, sourced guides to programs, credentials, and salaries.</li>
          <li>Evidence communication: figures and claims presented with their sources attached, never without.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Writing, evidence review and correction</h2>
        <p>My role on this publication follows a fixed process for every article, and it is described in full in our <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a>:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Define the reader's real question, not the keyword, before a single word is written.</li>
          <li>Verify every factual claim against reliable sources, and cite them where they can be checked.</li>
          <li>Check the limits and context of each finding: who it studied, what it cannot prove, and where it does not apply.</li>
          <li>Edit for accuracy in plain language, cutting anything that cannot be supported.</li>
          <li>Review published work on a rolling basis and correct errors openly when I find them or a reader reports one.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Selected completed learning</h2>
        <p>Course titles and issuing institutions are shown for context. Listing a course does not imply a degree, institutional endorsement, or a separate professional license. These are the parts of my continued study most relevant to behavioral psychology; my complete course list appears on my <a href="https://forensicpsychology.pro/author/hassam-shabbir/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">forensic psychology author profile</a>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>B.S. in Psychology, University of Sargodha</li>
          <li>Wesleyan University: Abnormal Psychology Specialization, including Introduction to Abnormal Psychology, History of Mental Illness, and Creating Behavioral Change</li>
          <li>Wesleyan University: Suicide Prevention</li>
          <li>University of Michigan: Understanding Psychosis</li>
          <li>University of Colorado: Providing Social, Emotional, Behavioral and Special Education Services in School</li>
          <li>University of Toronto: The Arts and Science of Relationships, Understanding Human Needs</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Selected independent work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Author of <em>Soch Say Sajjday Tak</em>, an Urdu book bringing psychology and Islamic teachings into conversation around mental noise, rumination, mindfulness, attention, and spiritual wellbeing.</li>
          <li>Founder of Rise Above Minds, a nonprofit sharing mental health and psychology education with children and communities.</li>
          <li>Writing portfolio of more than 1,000 articles across healthcare, education, technology, and other fields.</li>
          <li>Trained more than 400 professionals in AI and prompt engineering.</li>
          <li>Author of SEO and GEO eBooks and a Prompt Playbook.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Articles by Hassam Shabbir</h2>
        <p>Every guide links to its sources, publication date, evidence-review date, and editorial standards. Articles are listed from newest to oldest.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/what-is-behavioral-psychology/">What Is Behavioral Psychology? Definition and Basics</a> <span>November 3, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/degrees/">Behavioral Psychology Degree: The Complete Guide</a> <span>November 2, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/degrees/ms-behavioral-psychology/">MS in Behavioral Psychology: Degrees, Careers, Salary</a> <span>November 1, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/degrees/online-behavioral-psychology-degree/">Online Behavioral Psychology Degree Programs</a> <span>October 31, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/degrees/masters-in-behavioral-psychology/">Master's in Behavioral Psychology: Programs Guide</a> <span>October 30, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/degrees/phd-in-behavioral-psychology/">PhD in Behavioral Psychology: Programs and Careers</a> <span>October 29, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/careers/">Behavioral Psychology Jobs: Careers and Salaries</a> <span>October 28, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/behavioral-perspective-psychology/">The Behavioral Perspective in Psychology Explained</a> <span>October 27, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/behavioral-psychology-examples/">Behavioral Psychology Examples in Everyday Life</a> <span>October 26, 2026</span></li>
          <li><a href="/behavioral-science-vs-psychology/">Behavioral Science vs Psychology: What's Different?</a> <span>October 25, 2026</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Follow the evidence behind every article</h2>
        <p>I welcome corrections and source updates. If you spot an error, an outdated figure, or a claim that needs a better source, tell me through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and I will review it. Accuracy is a process, and readers are part of it.</p>

        <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/hassam_shabbir_official/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram: @hassam_shabbir_official</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.threads.net/@hassam_shabbir_official" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Threads: @hassam_shabbir_official</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hassam-shabbir-sxo/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn: Hassam Shabbir</a></li>
        </ul>

        <div class="boundary-box" role="note">
          <h2>Educational writing is not individual professional advice</h2>
          <p>Everything on this site is general education about behavioral psychology. It does not create a psychologist-patient relationship, it does not diagnose conditions, and it does not give treatment advice. If you are looking for help with a mental health concern, please consult a qualified professional. The <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> page explains this in full and lists emergency resources for readers in the United States.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .kicker {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--purple, #7c3aed);
      margin: 0 0 14px;
    }
    .boundary-box {
      margin-top: 48px;
      background: #f6f4f1;
      border: 1px solid #d9d2c6;
      border-left: 5px solid var(--purple, #7c3aed);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 26px 28px;
    }
    .boundary-box h2 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 20px; }
    .boundary-box p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
